# Patterns here are matched against the whole context-relative path, so a bare
# "node_modules" only excludes the root one. On Windows, pnpm creates per-package
# junctions under packages/*/node_modules whose targets are absolute host paths
# (F:\...); copying those into a Linux image leaves dangling links that break
# workspace resolution. Match at any depth instead.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
data
artifacts
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.pnpm-store
*.cpuprofile
.perfprof*
.questprof
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
